VeridianOS: KParts: handle QTemporaryFile::open() failures

GCC reported ignoring return value of 'bool QTemporaryFile::open()'
[-Wunused-result] at src/readonlypart.cpp:181 and src/readwritepart.cpp:209
and :247. Real bugs: when the temporary file could not be created (full or
read-only temp directory), QTemporaryFile::fileName() is empty and the code
carried on with an empty local path:

- ReadOnlyPartPrivate::openRemoteFile() started a KIO::file_copy() to an
  empty destination URL. It now logs the error with KPARTSLOG and emits
  canceled(errorString) (as the job-error path does), without starting the
  copy.
- ReadWritePartPrivate::prepareSaving() stored the empty path and marked it
  as a temp file. It now logs the error, leaves m_file empty and m_bTemp
  false; saveFile() then fails on the empty local path and save() emits
  canceled(), as it does for any other save failure.
- ReadWritePart::saveToUrl() went on to hard-link to an empty path. It now
  logs the error and returns false, the result it already returns when the
  hard link fails.

Behaviour is unchanged when the temporary file can be created.

diff -ru a/src/readonlypart.cpp b/src/readonlypart.cpp
--- a/src/readonlypart.cpp	2026-10-08 17:27:16.273002812 -0400
+++ b/src/readonlypart.cpp	2026-10-08 17:27:16.288642400 -0400
@@ -178,7 +178,13 @@
     }
     QTemporaryFile tempFile(QDir::tempPath() + QLatin1Char('/') + m_metaData.pluginId() + QLatin1String("XXXXXX") + extension);
     tempFile.setAutoRemove(false);
-    tempFile.open();
+    if (!tempFile.open()) {
+        qCWarning(KPARTSLOG) << "Could not create a temporary file for" << m_url << ":" << tempFile.errorString();
+        m_bTemp = false;
+        m_file.clear();
+        Q_EMIT q->canceled(tempFile.errorString());
+        return;
+    }
     m_file = tempFile.fileName();
 
     QUrl destURL = QUrl::fromLocalFile(m_file);
